              <run fontsize="10" bold="false" fontcolor="#173347">Crash types are mutually exclusive and include cars: car-on-car crashes are half of injury crashes but rarely fatal; single-car crashes are the largest group of fatal crashes. The grid compares fatal shares with and without each road user. Hover for 95% intervals. Calculated in the notebook.</run>
